From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 17:17:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 49/65] ci: fire the branch-filtered workflows on integration,
 not main (gcp-75ed)

Every workflow that carries a branch filter on this fork was scoped
`branches: [main]`, but no work on this rig ever touches main. Polecats
branch from `integration`, the refinery merges into `integration`, and
that is where every fork commit lands. The result was a CI config that
gated exactly the branch nobody's PR targets and never ran on the branch
all work flows through -- the structural reason integration rot (e.g.
the no-bare-bd guard red since 2026-07-31) went unnoticed until someone
ran the suite by hand.

This REPLACES `main` with `integration` in the six branch filters rather
than adding integration alongside it. main here is a pure upstream
mirror -- `git log upstream/main..origin/main` is empty -- so running the
fork's CI there would test upstream's tree on a branch nobody develops
on: noise, not coverage. Three files carry filters and change (ci.yml,
codeql.yml, pack-release-compatibility.yml, two lines each);
supported-pack-nightly.yml and gascity-pack-inference.yml have no branch
filter and deliberately do not gain one -- they are schedule /
workflow_dispatch only. `schedule:` blocks, `runs-on:` labels, and
pack-release-compatibility.yml's `paths:` filters are untouched.

Nothing is committed to main, by design: for `push` and `pull_request`
GitHub evaluates the workflow file from the triggering ref, so
integration's own copy governs integration work. Workflow registration
follows from the file existing on the default branch, which is already
true in upstream's version and needs no edit of ours.

Validation: all six filters now read `[integration]` and none read
`[main]`; the three files still parse under yaml.safe_load; the diff on
pack-release-compatibility.yml is the two branches lines and nothing
else; go build, go vet, go test -race, golangci-lint and
validate_registry.py all clean. The pack pytest suite is unchanged from
baseline -- 2 failed / 814 passed, with the same two failures
(test_formula_assets claim-command subprocess timeouts) reproduced on
the unmodified integration tip 6a9d06f. Filed separately.

Follow-up: the end-to-end proof (a run actually appearing for an
integration-targeted push) can only be observed after this merges.
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml                         | 4 ++--
 .github/workflows/codeql.yml                     | 4 ++--
 .github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml | 4 ++--
 3 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 382d94a..ebc8ff8 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -2,9 +2,9 @@ name: CI
 
 on:
   pull_request:
-    branches: [main]
+    branches: [integration]
   push:
-    branches: [main]
+    branches: [integration]
 
 permissions:
   contents: read
diff --git a/.github/workflows/codeql.yml b/.github/workflows/codeql.yml
index 1475e91..2199766 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/codeql.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/codeql.yml
@@ -2,9 +2,9 @@ name: CodeQL
 
 on:
   pull_request:
-    branches: [main]
+    branches: [integration]
   push:
-    branches: [main]
+    branches: [integration]
   schedule:
     - cron: "37 3 * * 1"
 
diff --git a/.github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml b/.github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml
index cd29f63..b651cf3 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml
@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@ name: Pack Release Compatibility
 
 on:
   pull_request:
-    branches: [main]
+    branches: [integration]
     paths:
       - registry.toml
       - scripts/pack_release_compat.py
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ on:
       - .github/workflows/pack-release-compatibility.yml
       - "*/pack.toml"
   push:
-    branches: [main]
+    branches: [integration]
     paths:
       - registry.toml
       - scripts/pack_release_compat.py
-- 
